# 📘 Agile Documentation

## Azure Demand Forecasting & Capacity Optimization System

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project was developed using **Agile methodology**, following a sprint-based approach.
The system focuses on forecasting Azure resource demand and optimizing capacity using machine learning and dashboards.

---

## 🧠 Agile Methodology Used

* Sprint-based development
* Incremental delivery
* Continuous testing & improvement
* Defect tracking and resolution

---

## 📋 Product Backlog

| ID   | Task                     | Priority |
| ---- | ------------------------ | -------- |
| PB-1 | Load dataset             | High     |
| PB-2 | Data cleaning            | High     |
| PB-3 | Feature engineering      | High     |
| PB-4 | Model training           | High     |
| PB-5 | Model evaluation         | High     |
| PB-6 | Forecast generation      | Medium   |
| PB-7 | Power BI dashboard       | Medium   |
| PB-8 | Streamlit dashboard      | Medium   |
| PB-9 | Capacity recommendations | High     |

---

## 🗓️ Sprint Planning

### 🔹 Sprint 1 (Data Preparation)

* Dataset loading
* Missing value handling
* Datetime standardization

### 🔹 Sprint 2 (Feature Engineering)

* Lag features (t-1, t-7, t-30)
* Rolling averages
* Capacity metrics

### 🔹 Sprint 3 (Model Development)

* Model training
* Model evaluation (RMSE, MAE, MAPE)
* Model selection

### 🔹 Sprint 4 (Deployment & Visualization)

* Forecast generation (30 days)
* Power BI dashboard
* Streamlit deployment
* Capacity recommendations

---

## 👤 User Stories

* As a data analyst, I want clean data so that analysis is accurate
* As a data scientist, I want features so that model performs well
* As a system, I want to predict demand so that future planning is possible
* As a manager, I want dashboards so that decisions can be made easily
* As a planner, I want capacity suggestions so that cost is optimized

---

## 🧪 Testing Approach

* Unit testing for data pipeline
* Validation of feature engineering
* Model evaluation using metrics
* Dashboard validation

👉 Supported by:

* Unit Test Plan
* Defect Tracker

---

## 🐞 Defect Management

* Issues tracked using Defect Tracker
* Categorized into: Data, Functional, UI
* Resolved across sprints
* Priority-based handling (High/Medium/Low)

---

## 🔄 Sprint Review

* Sprint 1: Data cleaned successfully
* Sprint 2: Features engineered
* Sprint 3: Model achieved high accuracy (MAPE 0.43%)
* Sprint 4: Dashboard deployed successfully

---

